2026-11-06T01:01:13.0675631Z             "body": "This draft adds the frontend Phase 2 identity, learning, authoring and account-lifecycle flows, plus whole-operation writer admission. Customer sign-in uses database sessions; explicit same-origin handlers issue audience-specific API credentials. Public catalog data is separated from private learning, access and playback responses. Approved deletion/export and paid-course archival policies are implemented.\n\nCourse PR #5/#6 and Community PR #4/#5 have merged normally. The released P2 contract bundle pins Course `3c0a0d6e` and Community `1ce696a7`; both exact API mains pass required post-merge quality, PostgreSQL/operator and native checks. The full 44-entry compatibility review preserves historical v1 files and enrollment-event bytes. Exact Git/archive/source/review verification passes at frontend `ab34cf9b`.\n\nPR #91 is consumed unchanged. PR #92 (`56d64fe`) is a real source predecessor with its execution core and original evidence preserved; this branch adds whole-cron/direct-worker admission and independent PII maintenance.\n\nRecorded validation includes 2,539 unit tests, 43 actual identity entry-point cases, 33 identity/lifecycle database cases, 19 export-lifecycle database tests, four actual authoring cases, and six actual Course-backed desktop/mobile learner cases. Local provider edges are owned fixtures and are identified in the evidence. Frontend CI at `ab34cf9b` passes quality/unit, build, audit and gateway/platform including strict native verification. Browser installation failed because locked Playwright 1.59.1 does not support the selected Ubuntu 26.04 runner; the matrix is being pinned to 24.04. The PostgreSQL 18 bootstrap fixture still fails during configuration and is under correction. Earlier failed attempts remain retained.\n\nThis draft is incomplete. Historical deployment/source/configuration classification and full provider effect reconciliation are still being integrated. The pending-SQL coordinator currently has an owned-fixture call site; the real operator release driver must still connect it to API migration/runtime and compatible frontend promotion under continuous locks. Final required frontend CI, immutable candidate qualification, actual Google/Resend/Mux and deployed authoring/learning/access/lifecycle/a11y/regression evidence remain open. P2-12 and G2 are unaccepted.\n\nNo staging SQL, provider/credential mutation, schedule activation, frontend promotion or production activation has occurred in this goal. Dardan must start the concrete reviewed staging release under the single-operator policy. Phase 3, paid-course checkout, Community member features and monitoring remain excluded.\n\nThe execution tracker, current checkpoint and `docs/api-integration/phase2-goal.md` link the source-bound evidence and remaining conditions.",
